# Review dependencies before adding them

Prefer platform APIs and code already in this repository for small features.
Do not add a package when a short local implementation is enough.

Before adding or upgrading a PackageReference:

- Inspect the package and its transitives for extra shared frameworks,
  especially `Microsoft.AspNetCore.App` in ControlApp.
- ControlApp is a framework-dependent WPF app. It must require only
  `Microsoft.NETCore.App` and `Microsoft.WindowsDesktop.App`.
- After publish, confirm the embedded runtimeconfig still lists those two
  frameworks at the `10.0.0` baseline and does not mention ASP.NET.

```xml
<!-- BAD: a desktop HTTP cache that silently requires ASP.NET Core -->
<PackageReference Include="Nefarius.HttpClient.LiteDbCache" Version="2.5.0" />

<!-- GOOD: keep the feature in-repo when the package graph is heavier than the need -->
```
